  data:  # 5a3f
    kind: work_item  # 5a3f
    title: "calls-edge src endpoint resolves to wrong same-base-name sibling method (506 edges out-of-span; 504 attributed to same-named peer in same file)"  # 5a3f
    status: todo_hard  # 5a3f
    priority: 0  # 5a3f
    parent:  # 5a3f
    tags:  # 5a3f
    - dogfood  # 5a3f
    - dogfood_tranche_05  # 5a3f
    isbefore: []  # 5a3f
    duplicate_of: []  # 5a3f
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 5a3f
    pr_ref:  # 5a3f
    description: "506 of 110510 'calls' edges (with non-null line) have a src method whose span does NOT contain the edge's line; in 504/506 (99.6%) the call line is actually owned by a DIFFERENT method/function with the SAME base name in the same file. The call-graph src is attributed to the wrong same-named symbol. All 506 are type=calls, origin=['python'], src kind=method. 100% of attributed src base names have multiplicity >1 in their file. Scope: 506 edges, 201 distinct src methods, 68 files (top base names: analyze 36, compose 12, _build 10, create 8, to_dict 7). Concrete: edge src=python:.../io_boundary.py:939-954:BoundaryMap.to_dict:method dst=...:266-277:is_high_risk:function line=863 — but BoundaryMap.to_dict spans 939-954; the true owner of line 863 is IoChain.to_dict (855-870). NOT a stable_id collision (node IDs are distinct by span); the EDGE's src endpoint resolves to the wrong same-named peer. Consequence: call graph asserts X calls Y where X does not contain the call site; an LLM agent attributes behavior to the wrong method."  # 5a3f
    fields: {}  # 5a3f
- op: discuss  # 2875
  at: '2026-06-06T04:10:25Z'  # 2875
  by: agent  # 2875
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2875
  clock: 2  # 2875
  nonce: '2875'  # 2875
  message: "Materialized from dogfood tranche 05 (F81.A1 / anon-card-014). Mechanism: calls-edge src endpoint resolves to wrong same-base-name sibling. Evidence: frozen substrate.json — 506/110510 calls edges out-of-span; concrete probe at io_boundary.py:939-954 (BoundaryMap.to_dict) vs true owner IoChain.to_dict at 855-870, call line 863. Magnitude: 506 edges, 201 src methods, 68 files; 504/506 (99.6%) attributed to same-base-name peer; 100% of src base names have multiplicity >1. Blind severity 5/5, reproduced on frozen substrate (read-only join, no injection). RELATED_BUT_DISTINCT from INV-majal (Go local-var-as-method-reference, holding), INV-mofav (Python nested-fn/bare-name-call drops, satisfied), and the various analyzer single-value-dict same-name resolution items (Go/Rust/verilog, done) — those are node-level/analyzer resolution defects; this is an edge-attribution defect where the calls EDGE src endpoint resolves to the wrong same-named peer in the same file."  # 2875
- op: discuss  # 8fbf
  at: '2026-06-06T10:35:52Z'  # 8fbf
  by: agent  # 8fbf
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8fbf
  clock: 3  # 8fbf
  nonce: 8fbf  # 8fbf
  message: "Re-confirmed on a full behavior map and root-caused with fresh repro (blind-severity-derived priority signal: P0). 1084/110510 edges (1.0%) have edge.line outside their src symbol's span; 804 land inside a DIFFERENT same-file symbol, and 647 of those (80%) are between symbols sharing the same last name segment (__post_init__/to_dict/from_dict). Root cause: Python call ownership resolved through a bare-name-keyed symbol_by_name dict at py.py:776 — two same-named symbols overwrite each other, the survivor owns ALL such calls, the overwritten sibling's calls VANISH. Fresh 'hypergumbo run' on a two-class fixture (each with __post_init__) emits exactly one calls edge: one class's call is misattributed to the other and the other's real call is entirely lost. Fix: key on (name, span)/scope-qualified identity."  # 8fbf
- op: discuss  # e13b
  at: '2026-06-08T03:21:43Z'  # e13b
  by: agent  # e13b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e13b
  clock: 4  # e13b
  nonce: e13b  # e13b
  message: "Re-surfaced in dogfooding tranche 10 (U07, F190.A1, severity 4). Same mechanism, broader scope: 653 calls/instantiates/references edges credited to the wrong caller via same-simple-name collapse (edge.line outside src.span). This item records 506 'calls' edges; the tranche-10 count of 653 includes instantiates + references too. Fix: fix the call-site->enclosing-symbol resolver to disambiguate same-simple-name methods by span (py.py)."  # e13b
- op: discuss  # 8825
